.TH LINUXSHARE-CLI 1 "September 2026" "linux-screen-share 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linuxshare-cli \- share your Linux screen as a virtual webcam
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxshare-cli
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxshare-cli
captures your screen under X11 or Wayland and pipes it into a
.B v4l2loopback
virtual camera device (for example
.IR /dev/video0 ).
The virtual camera can then be selected as a webcam in Microsoft Teams,
Zoom, Slack, Google Meet and any other application that reads a V4L2
device.
.PP
The session type is auto-detected from
.B $XDG_SESSION_TYPE
(falling back to
.B $WAYLAND_DISPLAY
and
.BR $DISPLAY ).
Under X11 the screen is grabbed with
.BR ffmpeg 's
.B x11grab
input. Under Wayland the capture is performed via
.B xdg-desktop-portal
and
.BR PipeWire ,
which will prompt you to choose the screen or window to share.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-display " NAME"
Display/output to share (default: auto-detect the primary output). Only
meaningful under X11; on Wayland the output is chosen through the portal.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " /dev/videoN"
The v4l2loopback device to write to (default: first available loopback
device).
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Capture framerate in frames per second (default: 30).
.TP
.B \-\-list-displays
List available displays/outputs and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Run a dependency check and exit with a non-zero status if a required
dependency is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose/debug output on standard error.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B ffmpeg\fR,
.B v4l2loopback-dkms\fR,
.B pipewire\fR,
.B xdg-desktop-portal
and, for Wayland capture,
.B gstreamer
with the
.B good
plugin set.
.SH SIGNALS
On
.B SIGINT
(Ctrl+C) or
.B SIGTERM
the capture process is terminated cleanly, and the
.B v4l2loopback
module remains loaded; manage it separately as an administrator.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/linuxshare/config.json
Settings shared with the GUI application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start sharing the primary screen:
.B linuxshare-cli
.TP
Share a specific X11 output at 60 fps:
.B linuxshare-cli --display HDMI-1 --fps 60
.TP
List displays:
.B linuxshare-cli --list-displays
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on error (missing dependencies, no device, capture failure).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR pw-record (1)
.SH AUTHOR
LinuxShare Contributors
